id: pm-gh1554
title: "GH-1554: resume bounded activity reads from a stable event window"
description: The October23 report shows activity limit truncation without a cursor or fixed-window recovery under concurrent writers. Reproduce current producer semantics and implement a stable bounded continuation or explicit fixed-window consistency recovery. Include the since-to-from flag recovery papercut.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: context-management,"gh:1554",sdk
created_at: "2026-10-23T07:33:56.767Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T12:38:38.222Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-24T12:38:36.866Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-24T12:38:36.866Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: A current temporary-tracker regression proves the omitted event set under concurrent writes; Continuation or fixed-window recovery is bounded and stable for timestamp ties; SDK CLI and MCP share the same completeness contract and since misuse points to from.
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Added opaque after cursors bound to a frozen query clock, workspace, projection/filter semantics and unchanged matching content. Preserve tied events by position, expose page/window metadata, refuse changed matching sets, isolate nested calendar cursors, align shell completion and preserve since-to-from intent."
expected_result: Recover every omitted matching event exactly once in bounded pages while later out-of-window writes continue; disclose and safely refuse unsupported matching-set changes.
actual_result: "All four activity projections recover complete tied-event sets; later writers remain outside the pinned window, backdated matching writes refuse stale cursors, CLI/MCP parity and malformed-cursor controls pass. The linked activity suite passes53 tests, calendar peer suite38, and five identical pre-fix completeness cases fail as expected. Full coverage/static and hosted review remain pending merge gates."
